---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is Virne?',
    a: 'Virne is a simulator and benchmark for resource allocation in Network Function Virtualization, unifying traditional and reinforcement learning based algorithms behind a common, Gymnasium-compatible interface. The benchmark paper was accepted at ICLR 2026 and the code is Apache-2.0 licensed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which problems does Virne cover?',
    a: 'Virtual Network Embedding (VNE), Virtual Network Function (VNF) placement, service function chain (SFC) deployment, and 5G network slicing. Simulations span cloud, edge, and 5G environments with user-defined topologies, resources, and service requirements.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many algorithms are included?',
    a: 'Over 30 registered algorithms, of which more than 10 are non-learning: exact, heuristic, meta-heuristic, and learning-based families all share one interface, and new solvers plug in via module customization.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I install Virne?',
    a: 'Install from PyPI with Python 3.12 or newer: pip install virne. Documentation, examples, and source code are at virne.readthedocs.io and github.com/GeminiLight/virne.',
  },
];
---

<div class="faq">
  {faqs.map((f) => (
    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>{f.q}</summary>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </details>
  ))}
</div>

<style>
  .faq-item {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .faq-item:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 16px;
    padding: 14px 4px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 15px;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::after {
    content: '+';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    transition: transform 200ms ease, color 160ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] summary::after {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }

  .faq-item[open] summary {
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }

  .faq-item summary:hover {
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }

  .faq-item p {
    padding: 0 4px 16px;
    max-width: 72ch;
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
</style>
